# Loop head merges a path that continues without writing

Verifies the loop head merges the unchanged path with the written path. The
first iteration continues before writing, so the second reads the original
centimeter-millimeter value and prints `11mm`.

>>> source
let a: int[] = [10mm]

for (i in 0..2) {
    if (i == 0) {
        continue
    }
    print(a[0] + 1mm)
    a[0] = 2cm
}

<<< stdout
11mm

<<< stderr
